{%- comment -%}
  snippets/kj-mark.liquid
  {% render 'kj-mark' %}                       → the KJ ellipse mark
  {% render 'kj-mark', mark: 'lada' %}         → the Lada script wordmark
  {% render 'kj-mark', mark: 'lada', label: 'Lada by Khan Jee' %}

  Both are <use> references into kj-svg-defs, so the geometry ships once.
  Colour comes from currentColor — set it on the parent, never here.
  Pass label to make the mark meaningful to a screen reader; leave it off
  and the mark is decorative, which is right when readable text sits
  beside it.

  The Lada mark is a monoline script, so it is stroked rather than
  filled — the stroke attributes live on the <symbol> and scale with it,
  which is what keeps the mark looking like itself at any size.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign m = mark | default: 'kj'
  if m == 'lada'
    assign href = '#lada-path'
    assign ratio = 'kj-mark--lada'
  else
    assign href = '#kj-path'
    assign ratio = 'kj-mark--kj'
  endif
-%}

<svg class="kj-mark {{ ratio }}{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
     {% if label %}role="img" aria-label="{{ label | escape }}"{% else %}aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"{% endif %}>
  <use href="{{ href }}"></use>
</svg>
